{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he erected there an altar, and called it El Elohei Yisrael.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): Jacob called the name of the altar by the name of the King, as a memorial of the miracle. And likewise did Moses our teacher, peace be upon him, call it ״YHWH is my banner״ (ה' נסי)." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: the verse is to be expounded that the God of Israel called Jacob 'El.' And so the masters of truth expounded: the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Jacob, 'You are a god (elohah) among the supernal beings, and I am a god among the lower beings.' And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'the image (ikaron) of Jacob is engraved upon the Throne of Glory' — the intention being that the Shekhinah dwells in the land of Israel. And from this Balaam said (Numbers 23:8): ״מה אקוב לא קבה אל״ — 'How shall I curse, whom El has not cursed?' And he said this concerning Jacob, that even in the hour of his anger he did not curse but only seethed (אפם)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {1 "The heading reads <b>וע\"ד</b> (ועל דרך), continuing the lemma from comment 0; rendered as 'And by way of' accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:30.254645355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}